{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/arrayslice\/reservecapacity(_:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ArraySlice\/reserveCapacity(_:)"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ArraySlice"]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reserveCapacity"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"minimumCapacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Int","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The requested number of elements to store.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"minimumCapacity"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you are adding a known number of elements to an array, use this method","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to avoid multiple reallocations. This method ensures that the array has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unique, mutable, contiguous storage, with space allocated for at least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the requested number of elements.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calling the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"text":" method on an array with bridged storage","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"triggers a copy to contiguous storage even if the existing storage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has room to store "},{"code":"minimumCapacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" elements."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For performance reasons, the size of the newly allocated storage might be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"greater than the requested capacity. Use the array’s "},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to determine the size of the new storage."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Preserving an Array’s Geometric Growth Strategy","anchor":"Preserving-an-Arrays-Geometric-Growth-Strategy","level":1,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you implement a custom data structure backed by an array that grows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dynamically, naively calling the "},{"code":"reserveCapacity(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method can lead"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to worse than expected performance. Arrays need to follow a geometric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allocation pattern for appending elements to achieve amortized"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constant-time performance. The "},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type’s "},{"code":"append(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"append(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" methods take care of this detail for you, but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"reserveCapacity(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" allocates only as much space as you tell it to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(padded to a round value), and no more. This avoids over-allocation, but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can result in insertion not having amortized constant-time performance."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following code declares "},{"code":"values","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", an array of integers, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"addTenQuadratic()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" function, which adds ten more values to the "},{"code":"values","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array on each call."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["  var values: [Int] = [0, 1, 2, 3]","","  \/\/ Don't use 'reserveCapacity(_:)' like this","  func addTenQuadratic() {","      let newCount = values.count + 10","      values.reserveCapacity(newCount)","      for n in values.count..<newCount {","          values.append(n)","      }","  }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The call to "},{"code":"reserveCapacity(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" increases the "},{"code":"values","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" array’s capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by exactly 10 elements on each pass through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addTenQuadratic()"},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"is linear growth. Instead of having constant time when averaged over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"many calls, the function may decay to performance that is linear in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values.count"},{"type":"text","text":". This is almost certainly not what you want."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases like this, the simplest fix is often to simply remove the call"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and let the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"append(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method grow the array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for you."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["  func addTen() {","      let newCount = values.count + 10","      for n in values.count..<newCount {","          values.append(n)","      }","  }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need more control over the capacity of your array, implement your"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"own geometric growth strategy, passing the size you compute to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the number of elements in the array."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Reserves enough space to store the specified number of elements.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"extendedModule":"Swift","platforms":[{"introducedAt":"8.0","name":"iOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"8.0","name":"iPadOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"13.0","name":"Mac Catalyst","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"10.10","beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false},{"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"9.0","beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false},{"introducedAt":"1.0","deprecated":false,"name":"visionOS","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"introducedAt":"2.0","deprecated":false,"name":"watchOS","unavailable":false,"beta":false}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reserveCapacity"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"method","title":"reserveCapacity(_:)","externalID":"s:s10ArraySliceV15reserveCapacityyySiF"},"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"title":"Swift","abstract":[{"text":"Build apps using a powerful open language.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swift"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/ArraySlice":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/arrayslice","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ArraySlice"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A slice of an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContiguousArray"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ArraySlice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ArraySlice","title":"ArraySlice","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ArraySlice"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/ArraySlice/reserveCapacity(_:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reserveCapacity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Reserves enough space to store the specified number of elements.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"reserveCapacity(_:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ArraySlice\/reserveCapacity(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/arrayslice\/reservecapacity(_:)"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Int":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A signed integer value type.","type":"text"}],"title":"Int","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Int","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/int","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Int"}}}